# While the `:` line's as-you-type completion popup shows, one Esc
# abandons the line, popup and all; the next keys are Normal mode's.
# Neovim 0.12.5 (`nvim --clean`, wildoptions=pum):
# `:tabn<Tab><Esc>iX<Esc>` -> buffer "Xhello" (Esc abandons the line).
write t.txt "hello\n"
open t.txt
command editor.use_vim
key :
type tabn
expect screen contains "tabnext"
key esc
type iX
key esc
command file.save
expect file t.txt contains "Xhello\n"
